MID_LGV_1_M07_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Kai_m01_001: I'm still doing my drill of running full speed through\nthe crowds.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Kai_m01_002: Once I got good at it, I started paying attention to my\nsurroundings, and what everyone else was doing.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Kai_m01_003: Now, all I end up doing is helping people out or\nsaying "hey" to people I know.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Kai_m01: <BLN>I need to focus...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bel_m01_001: A fellow prisoner told me the Twin Jewels of Arago\ncompeted in the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bel_m01_002: What in the world were Nathan and Creek doing in\nthe arena?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bel_m01_003: Up to something again, was he?
MID_LGA_1_M07_Bel_m01: <BLN>What in the world...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dit_m01_001: How might you become as strong as I am?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dit_m01_002: I cannot say. My blade strikes how I will it. That\nis all.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Dit_m01: <BLN>You wish to know something?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tal_m01_001: So, win the Heroic Games and the Sovereign grants\nyou a wish, eh?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tal_m01_002: If I ruled a country, maybe I'd start granting\nwishes too.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tal_m01_003: Hearing people's wants and hopes, their innermost\ndesires... Sounds pretty damn interesting, no?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tal_m01_004: Plus, imagine being the one to bring someone's\ndream to life. Haha! Yeah, I'll definitely do it.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Tal_m01: <BLN>That's it, I've decided.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Orh_m01_001: The capital is truly astounding, brimming with both\ncrowds and water, everywhere!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Orh_m01_002: But I need to be careful when I get too close to\nthe lakeshore around the city.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Orh_m01_003: If I find myself on soft ground, I'll sink before I\nknow it...and just keep sinking!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Orh_m01: <BLN>So troublesome!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Seo_m01_001: There are places in the land of Dagda where it is\nforbidden to set foot.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Seo_m01_002: One such place is Cybele. Another is the forbidden\nland at the western edge of the Chronos Desert.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Seo_m01_003: Both of these have ties to the People of the White\nEgg, which makes me uneasy.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Seo_m01: <BLN>It does not sit well with me.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Led_m01_001: The more time I spend in the capital, the more I'm\nreminded how incredible Kalla is.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Led_m01_002: Even the novice priests at her temple have more skill\nthan the bards in town.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Led_m01_003: And the most expensive cosmetics on sale in Dagsion\nwould go for a pittance in Caelus.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Led_m01_004: Though the capital does have superior cuisine going\nfor it. I have no idea how they make such good food.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Led_m01: <BLN>As I'm thinking about it...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Anh_m01_001: The other day, I was telling fortunes on the street,\nand a girl I didn't know gave me some food.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Anh_m01_002: She said it wasn't payment, just that she'd worked\nhard to make it and wanted me to try some.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Anh_m01_003: Then she ran away down the street. What do you\nthink that was all about?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Anh_m01_004: <NCA>Suggest the girl thought Anatolia looked hungry.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Anh_m01_005: <NCB>Suggest the girl wanted to support her.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Anh_m01_006: <ACA>I'm not so sure. As a Mediator, my physical needs\nshould not be outwardly visible.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Anh_m01_007: <ACB>If that's the case, then I should thank her.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Anh_m01: <BLN>What was that all about?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tia_m01_001: I was born in Arago, so it was lots of fun to see the\nknights of Arago in action!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tia_m01_002: I was surprised by their unusual strategies though.\nI'd figured they'd focus on more standard moves.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tia_m01_003: I expected the knights would stay faithful to their\ntraining fundamentals.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Tia_m01: <BLN>I was surprised...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Pet_m01_001: Everyone in the Heroic Games is so strong.\nIt's pretty impressive, but...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Pet_m01_002: I noticed someone really strange. Like they have this\nweird glare or something. I don't know how to put it.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Pet_m01: <BLN>It's just something I noticed, but...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hur_m01_001: Ugh. This guy tried hitting on me earlier. He did\nNOT know when to quit...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hur_m01_002: All I was doing was being polite, but he totally took it\nthe wrong way and thought I was attracted to him.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hur_m01_003: He was offering to buy me dinner! Honestly, stuff\nlike that is just so irritating!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Hur_m01: <BLN>Gross...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Max_m01_001: Hehehe! Who'd have guessed it? The Twin Jewels\nof Arago fighting in the arena!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Max_m01_002: I know they're big-shot generals, but still, it's not easy\njoining in this spectacle.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Max_m01_003: Makes me wonder what those Aragonian rats might\nbe up to...
MID_LGA_1_M07_Max_m01: <BLN>It's not easy...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gol_m01_001: Going out for a drink's not easy when you're my size!\nThe tavern doors are always too small.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gol_m01_002: I gotta hunch down to get through 'em—it's a pain in\nthe neck.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gol_m01_003: The other day after I'd gone drinking, I went to leave\nand ended up smashing through the wall.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gol_m01_004: Guess it worked out, though, since the entrance is a\nlot bigger now! Bwahaha!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Gol_m01: <BLN>No one gets it!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gat_m01_001: A person's true worth is tested when they face death.\nThat is as true in the arena as anywhere else.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gat_m01_002: If you wanted to judge someone's character, you\ncould watch how they act in the Heroic Games.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Gat_m01: <BLN>It's a certainty.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dan_m01_001: You can tell much about a contestant by seeing how\nthey spend the days before the match.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dan_m01_002: Some train, some return to their usual duties—some\nmay not do anything!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dan_m01_003: By observing their behavior in these times, one can\ncatch a glimpse into these fighters' true nature.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dan_m01_004: Ahh, if only there were a few more of me, I could\ninterview them all!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Dan_m01: <BLN>I'm so fascinated!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fab_m01_001: Ah, you. Well, perhaps this is good timing. I have a\nquestion to pose.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fab_m01_002: You have a goal, and in service of that goal, you\ncommand subordinates.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fab_m01_003: But how far will you go? Would you sacrifice their\nlives to achieve your goal?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fab_m01_004: <NCA>Ask about the point of the question.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fab_m01_005: <NCB>Flatly deny that you would do this.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fab_m01_006: <ACA>Hmm. A refusal to answer. Then let my question be\nthe starting point for your deliberations.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fab_m01_007: <ACB>A rote assertion. Your perspective on this is\nsimplistic and driven by emotion.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fab_m01_008: <ACB>But it seems that you believe this is the reason they\nadmire you. I do respect that you see them as equals.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Fab_m01: <BLN>I have a question.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Esm_m01_001: That Ursula from the Vandahl Trading Company...\nShe has an unusual scent about her.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Esm_m01_002: I think she probably came here from Fódlan, like\nSweetie and Fabio did.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Esm_m01_003: I wonder why she set up as a merchant, though. Does\nshe like it here all that much?
MID_LGA_1_M07_Esm_m01: <BLN>I wonder about her...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Urs_m01_001: I went to an art store for some paint supplies and\nsaw a missionary from Fódlan there.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Urs_m01_002: Does he paint too? I don't like sharing the same\nhobbies as someone who serves the church.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Urs_m01_003: From now on, I should send a runner from the\ncompany to procure my art supplies...
MID_LGA_1_M07_Urs_m01: <BLN>Does he paint too? Or...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sim_m01_001: I've known Talimun for a long time now. Job after\njob, I've been his right hand plenty of times.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sim_m01_002: Doesn't mean I'm tied to the company, though. If a\ncontract told me to take the company down, I would.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sim_m01_003: When most people hear that, they say I'm disloyal.\nWhat do you think?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sim_m01_004: <NCA>Tell him you're not sure. It has nothing to do with you.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sim_m01_005: <NCB>Tell him it's disloyal.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sim_m01_006: <ACA>Ha! Yeah, you get it. What happens between\nothers is THEIR business.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sim_m01_007: <ACB>In my world, "unbreakable allegiances" will get you\nkilled fast. Trusting people like that...it's naïve.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Sim_m01: <BLN>I am who I am.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lou_m01_001: I think I'm starting to understand why the people of\nDagsion buy what they do.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lou_m01_002: Goods that are common in other regions can feel\nniche and alluring to people of the capital.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lou_m01_003: They can't help their own curiosity. Heheh! I'll need\nto buy more stock of the "exotic" stuff.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Lou_m01: <BLN>I'm starting to get it!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fia_m01_001: There's something special about poetry. It acts as a\nwindow into its author's heart.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fia_m01_002: Through it, you can feel all kinds of emotions.\nGentleness, loneliness... It makes me think...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Fia_m01_003: If my memories do return, I still want to remember\nall the emotions I've felt as I am now...
MID_LGA_1_M07_Fia_m01: <BLN>If my memories do return to me...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Die_m01_001: Now that Orchel's been unmasked, people flock to\nher side everywhere she goes.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Die_m01_002: So foolish. They used to dismiss her as some\nkind of weird priest.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Die_m01_003: Some people are coming right up to her to propose.\nUgh. I have to keep her safe from these crowds.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Die_m01: <BLN>Now, more than ever...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lor_m01_001: Got some great training in today. I'll never forget\nwhat Ozin said...handle your weapon every day!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lor_m01_002: I have to be strong! I'm gonna take down the bad\nguys and stand up for what's right!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Lor_m01: <BLN>Gotta stay strong!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Set_m01_001: Warrior clans exist across the continent, like the\nHar Hali, the Chetaur, and the Asherah.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Set_m01_002: Writing stories and fables based on their cultures\nwill be an intriguing challenge.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Set_m01_003: Though getting stories out of anyone from the\nHar Hali might prove difficult.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Set_m01: <BLN>Very intriguing.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nin_m01_001: What was it I went out to purchase? It's eluding\nmemory—escaping it entirely.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nin_m01_002: Ah, you all... You don't remember either... Your\ncarefree existence... Why would you...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nin_m01_003: How about you? Do you know?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nin_m01_004: <NCA>Ask why YOU would know.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nin_m01_005: <NCB>Tell her it'll work out in the end.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nin_m01_006: <ACA>I sense a real cold from you.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nin_m01_007: <ACB>Oh, I sense the truth in that! Maybe I'll remember\nif I don't try so hard to remember.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Nin_m01: <BLN>What was it?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bon_m01_001: Perhaps I am biased due to my keen memory for\nthe faces from our homeland...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bon_m01_002: But there are so many fair maidens in Dagsion.\nTheir novelty only heightens their appeal.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bon_m01_003: Seeing such lovely sights makes me feel young\nagain. Ohoho...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bon_m01_004: <NCA>Tell him you're glad he's enjoying himself.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bon_m01_005: <NCB>Warn him not to get carried away.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bon_m01_006: <ACA>Indeed. A healthy appreciation for beauty is\na blessing.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bon_m01_007: <ACB>You think I would forget myself so? Hmph. I see that\nyou hold me in low esteem indeed.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Bon_m01_008: <ACB>Know that I merely appreciate the maidens from\nafar. A flower does not grow more lovely in the hand.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Bon_m01: <BLN>What a pleasing sight.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tob_m01_001: The soldiers we brought with us are keeping busy.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tob_m01_002: It's not much of a reward, but I'm thinkin' I might\ntreat 'em all to a feast sometime.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Tob_m01_003: They could croak any day—or I could! So we gotta\nenjoy ourselves while we're still around.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Tob_m01: <BLN>It's always somethin'.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lil_m01_001: It's my turn to cook at the barracks. I hate drawing\nchef duty.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lil_m01_002: But if I've gotta do it, I may as well cook up a meal\nthat'll shut up all the soldiers who usually rag on me.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Lil_m01: <BLN>This is the worst duty...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lys_m01_001: The Twin Jewels of Arago may not be of Saramis,\nbut I admire their commitment to their monarch.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lys_m01_002: I've observed their fighting styles closely so that I\nmight be inspired to achieve greater heights myself.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Lys_m01: <BLN>The Twin Jewels of Arago...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Buc_m01_001: Seeing Solel in the crowd, I was reminded of the\nold days.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Buc_m01_002: I remember him scowling down at the imperial army\nduring military parades. He's hardly changed a bit.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Buc_m01: <BLN>It reminded me of the old days.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sci_m01_001: Dagsion's abuzz about the pretty priest, but there's\nanother piece of news I picked up on.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sci_m01_002: The queen of Saramis and the Twin Jewels of Arago\nare competing. So, it's said a war may break out.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sci_m01_003: All of it has led some to conclude that the entire\ngames are a plot to blunt their militaries.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sci_m01_004: My lady has had her own doubts regarding the\nreason for the event. Perhaps I'd better investigate...
MID_LGA_1_M07_Sci_m01: <BLN>Dagsion's abuzz...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Moo_m01_001: The mechanisms in the arena blow my mind.\nHow do they recreate all those old battlefields?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Moo_m01_002: And how did they get that big stage set up in the\nfirst place? They must be using a waterwheel...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Moo_m01_003: I'm so curious now! Gah, I wish I could go poke\naround with no one else there.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Moo_m01: <BLN>It's wild.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Mic_m01_001: I've been training for a good long while, but I can't\nseem to build any nice-looking muscle.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Mic_m01_002: Personally, I'd like to get buff enough that people\ncould tell at a glance even from a distance.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Mic_m01: <BLN>It's not going well...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Oly_m01_001: I was chitchatting with some priests, and they asked\nwhether I wanted to be a vulkan.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Oly_m01_002: They said if I had strength enough to fight in the\ngames, I should do it. But that's not why I'm here!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Oly_m01_003: Besides, I don't want to be Kalla's sword. I want to\nbe her rose!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Oly_m01: <BLN>I'm after something different.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Naz_m01_001: Sha Lan still asks me all kindsa stuff that's none\nof her business.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Naz_m01_002: She says, "Are you eating properly?" or "Are you\nkeeping your clothes clean?"
MID_LGV_1_M07_Naz_m01_003: I'm doing just fine living outside the village!\nShe doesn't need to worry about it.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Naz_m01: <BLN>*sigh*
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sar_m01_001: Is everyone back in the village getting enough to eat?\nAre they wearing clean clothes? Sleeping properly?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sar_m01_002: I can't help but worry. These are important concerns.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Sar_m01: <BLN>I worry about everyone.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dai_m01_001: An old hunter a while back told me he had meat to\nshare. Then he put me to work helping him hunt!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dai_m01_002: If he needed help, he shoulda just come out and said\nso. No need to protect your pride, buddy.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Dai_m01_003: Still, it was some tasty meat! And it's always nice\nto go hunting with someone else!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Dai_m01: <BLN>I got to eat some tasty meat!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hal_m01_001: Plain coffee is so bitter! I can't even pretend to make\nmyself like it.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hal_m01_002: I do like it with milk and honey though. And I love a\ncup with a sweet snack. Is that maybe too indulgent?
MID_LGA_1_M07_Hal_m01: <BLN>It's not that I can't drink it, but...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Guj_m01_001: Dante came to me looking for story ideas, so I\nshared many a Guzran escapade!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Guj_m01_002: She threw up her hands and walked off, saying that\nI defied belief. That children made more sense!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Guj_m01_003: What a reaction! I mean, I was there for each of\nthese epic feats! Every detail, lived by ME!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Guj_m01: <BLN>She couldn't grasp it.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Yan_m01_001: One of the joys of travel is finding yourself in the\nproximity of truly local tipple!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Yan_m01_002: The wine of the south... The aged mead in the\nnorth... Nectars by different names!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Yan_m01_003: My wandering has bobbed and weaved all over the\ncontinent. I have many tales of drink and revelry!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Yan_m01: <BLN>Ha haaa!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Iio_m01_001: Nathan and Creek lived up to their reputation in\nthat recent match, that's for sure!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Iio_m01_002: {SetColor=Gray}Then again... Why'd they go for Orchel's mask?\nA terrible tactic for the celebrated generals...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_1_M07_Iio_m01_003: {SetColor=Gray}But their tactics are usually exemplary... Could it\nbe...that they were ordered to do that?{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGA_1_M07_Iio_m01: <BLN>It's a real mystery...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Pep_m01_001: We perceive more temple soldiers here. Are they\nhaving difficulty keeping the peace of late?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Pep_m01_002: Thieves in the shadows? Bloody treachery in the\ndark? Perhaps it's in the nature of vast cities.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Pep_m01: <BLN>Do we perceive it correctly?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Noc_m01_001: I'm trying to learn the ways of city life, but I'm\nfinding it harder than ever.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Noc_m01_002: When I ask people, they just tell me I can do\npretty much...as I please.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Noc_m01_003: Ugggh. What even is a city?!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Noc_m01: <BLN>I can't figure it out.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sop_m01_001: Lord Solel's statue is grand as it gets! Of course,\nthe actual Solel is a lot more extra-grand!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sop_m01_002: The wonderful sight of him is like a window into\nhis inner kindness. Or something like that!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Sop_m01_003: Anyone who's met him would get it!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Sop_m01: <BLN>Do you get it?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Cat_m01_001: The Twin Jewels of Arago live up to their name, but\nrumors about their king swirl with ugliness.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Cat_m01_002: Do they serve such a man because they feel they\nmust? Then I have their measure wrong.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Cat_m01_003: And if they don't grasp the situation at all, then\nthey're not even worth measuring.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Cat_m01: <BLN>I have their measure wrong.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ned_m01_001: The Heroic Games have brought a lot more shops\nto the capital, and food stalls too.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ned_m01_002: I don't care much for the meat dishes. I prefer the \nsweets, like those made with honey and dates.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ned_m01_003: I bet many of these shops and stalls will close after\nthe games end. But hopefully not.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Ned_m01: <BLN>Hopefully they stay here.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Zac_m01_001: I spotted some guy with some veggies. Good stuff!\nCan't stop drooling over 'em.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Zac_m01_002: Heh heh! And maybe if he finds himself alone...\nhe'll find he wants to just fork it all over!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Zac_m01: <BLN>Heh heh!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Maj_m01_001: Damn these people! Who do they think they ARE,\nfeasting like they're champions or something?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Maj_m01_002: Even the rats in the prison are gettin' plump.\nTasty too.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Maj_m01: <BLN>All these people!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ven_m01_001: Masks and ladies! Ladies and masks! Who cares?!\nBut it's the talk of the city lately. What swine!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ven_m01_002: We saw a rare match, as if those knights stepped\noff the pages of the War Chronicle of Hasdrubal!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ven_m01_003: All this prattling about how women look, or don't\nlook—it's pathetic and pointless!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Ven_m01: <BLN>Pathetic!
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ini_m01_001: There'll be nothing but disasters in store, thanks\nto the Order of Mithras.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ini_m01_002: They swindled me out of the money my family and\nfriends lent me—all for Ugo's Bow.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ini_m01_003: I can't go back to my people until I earn it back.\nAnd that means mercenary work...
MID_LGA_1_M07_Ini_m01: <BLN>Ugh...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Jas_m01_001: I can't get my head around noble Creek treating\nhis opponent like that.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Jas_m01_002: When I was in Arago, he was considered the\nmost wonderful fellow—a real gentleman.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Jas_m01: <BLN>What happened to him?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ale_m01_001: I was having the nicest time chatting with\nEsmeralda about her "Sweetie" a short while ago.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ale_m01_002: Then I said he seemed like a kind, great person. She\ngave me such an angry look! Yet...happy too?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Ale_m01_003: Then she stormed off and shouted, "I won't lose\nto you!" I thought we were friends!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Ale_m01: <BLN>What'd I say?
MID_LGV_1_M07_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Cen_m01_001: The vulkans in Aurora's temple are supporting the\nsmooth operation of the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Cen_m01_002: However, other temples' vulkans are doing otherwise.\nSome enter the contest, others hide their faces.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Cen_m01_003: It's unavoidable, I suppose. Vulkans are subordinate\nto the divine. They do what the gods ask of them.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Cen_m01: <BLN>They do what they're told...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Kir_m01_001: Damn! I saw someone who used to beg for a shot at\nworkin' for me. Now he's treatin' me all different...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Kir_m01_002: All my guys are gonna give me the cold shoulder\nonce they find out I've lost my whole treasure...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Kir_m01_003: I'll make 'em regret it! Every last one of 'em!
MID_LGA_1_M07_Kir_m01: <BLN>They're going to regret it...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nuz_m01_001: I have seen my duty through to the end. Now I\nreturn to being a simple Har Hali warrior.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nuz_m01_002: I must grow in wisdom so as not to repeat the\nmistakes of Bahr Vahn.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Nuz_m01: <BLN>I have much to learn.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gab_m01_001: There are some things you hate remembering,\nno matter how much time goes by.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gab_m01_002: And when you're an old man like me, you get to\nhave a lotta stuff like that piled up.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Gab_m01_003: But c'mon... Why'd he have to reappear here? Now?\nOf all times?
MID_LGA_1_M07_Gab_m01: <BLN>It's no joke.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lin_m01_001: The people of this city have long forgotten me.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Lin_m01_002: My name... My deeds... All has faded into oblivion.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Lin_m01: <BLN>All has faded into oblivion...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nat_m01_001: I'm surprised the games reeled in so many warriors\nI'd never even heard of.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Nat_m01_002: I don't think it would be an exaggeration to call this a\nhistoric gathering of Dagda's best.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Nat_m01: <BLN>The Heroic Games impress me.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hri_m01_001: Defeat after defeat last month! You almost have\nto laugh.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hri_m01_002: The sheen's really come off the Twin Jewels\nof Arago.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Hri_m01_003: I wouldn't be very proud to face my sister like this.
MID_LGA_1_M07_Hri_m01: <BLN>It's funny.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Miw_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_Miw_m01_001: Paradise... White Canyon Zanado... It eats people.\nSwallows them in an instant.
MID_LGV_1_M07_Miw_m01_002: But nobody ever believes the things I say...
MID_LGV_1_M07_Miw_m01_003: Do you believe what I'm telling you?
MID_LGA_1_M07_Miw_m01: <BLN>Paradise eats people...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B01_m01_001: I got to see the Twin Jewels of Arago. It was all I\nhoped for! The red-and-green team is unbeatable.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B01_m01_002: I should find a buddy and practice to be just like\nthem. Maybe my brother would be up for it.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B01_m01: <BLN>They're unbeatable!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B02_m01_001: Fruit makes for a pretty good snack to grab in\nbetween security shifts.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B02_m01_002: I might grab a bunch of jin ba jiao or a bag of ginji\nfruit to share with my comrades in arms.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B02_m01_003: Though some sweets coated with coffee-berry paste\nwould be good too... Wait, no, I'm distracting myself.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B02_m01: <BLN>Decisions, decisions...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B03_m01_001: It's always nice to find dishes made with ingredients\nfrom my homeland in a tavern here.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B03_m01_002: I like seeing the vegetables my people work hard\nto grow being enjoyed by others.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B03_m01_003: When I'm back home, I'll tell them all how much they\nloved it in the capital.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B03_m01: <BLN>It's a nice feeling.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B04_m01_001: Beauty must be its own trouble. I heard of a gorgeous\npriest who hid herself away behind a mask.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B04_m01_002: They say she could no longer bear the constant\nattention and flattery.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B04_m01_003: Hmmm... I envy her, yet in some ways I don't.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B04_m01: <BLN>A mask is an extreme solution.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B05_m01_001: I can't abide that Creek! My granddaughter has\nstarted saying she's going to marry him.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B05_m01_002: She's scarcely five years old! Much too young to\nthink of such things. Ahh, why did I take her along?
MID_LGA_1_M07_B05_m01: <BLN>I can't abide that man!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B06_m01_001: Cleaning, water carrying, more cleaning, manuscript\ncopying, even more cleaning... I'm at my wit's end!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B06_m01_002: But heavy burdens make for strong faith. I'll get\nsome sleep and redouble my efforts tomorrow!
MID_LGA_1_M07_B06_m01: <BLN>I'm at my wit's end!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B07_m01_001: My duties require me to travel to Yashiro Fort,\nbut it's so far from here.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B07_m01_002: There's some concern whether the local viceroy and\nmilitary will cooperate. Fingers crossed...
MID_LGA_1_M07_B07_m01: <BLN>Yashiro Fort is so far...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B08_m01_001: Credna's temple has been steadily drawing in\nworshippers. It must be that beautiful lead priest.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B08_m01_002: They're making a mockery of the faith! The temple\nought to turn them all away!
MID_LGA_1_M07_B08_m01: <BLN>This is an outrage!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B09_m01_001: I wonder if it's time to move on... I'd have to hire\nsome mercenaries to escort me, though.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B09_m01_002: I've been burned before, so this time I'll properly vet\nthem. A treacherous bodyguard is worse than none.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B09_m01: <BLN>It may be time to move on...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B10_m01_001: I go to the tavern every day. It's wonderful not to\nhave to cook for myself!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B10_m01_002: I owe it all to winning big on a bet I placed at the\nHeroic Games. I should thank that clan...
MID_LGA_1_M07_B10_m01: <BLN>I should thank them!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B11_m01_001: I've been putting in my time helping out for years.\nSo when will he let me take up the hammer?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B11_m01_002: I've been watching how Dad does it since I was born,\nbut he still says, "You've got a lot to learn!"
MID_LGV_1_M07_B11_m01_003: If I could just get some experience at the anvil,\nI could be crafting quality swords in no time!
MID_LGA_1_M07_B11_m01: <BLN>I've put in my time helping out!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B12_m01_001: Do you think it's true the chief executive of the\nVandahl Trading Company is from Feronia?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B12_m01_002: That's where I'm from! I never imagined I might be\nneighbors with someone so rich.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B12_m01: <BLN>We're practically neighbors.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B13_m01_001: Why are they making me survey the creatures living\nin the lake?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B13_m01_002: I'll ask the locals for information. Maybe I can put\ntogether a decent report without dirtying my hands.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B13_m01: <BLN>Why me?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B14_m01_001: That Saraminian ship is incredible. I wonder if they'd\nshare the secrets of how it was built.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B14_m01_002: Well, even if they would, I'd have to ask first.\nAnd they're way too scary for that.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B14_m01: <BLN>What an incredible ship...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B15_m01_001: From time to time, I see children playing around\nthe moored ships.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B15_m01_002: What will they do if some of that cargo falls on them,\nor they get tangled up in the lines?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B15_m01_003: I'll have to give them a good telling-off the next time\nI see them at the docks.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B15_m01: <BLN>I ought to tell them off!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B16_m01_001: I managed to completely sell out of my inventory!\nAnd it feels amazing.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B16_m01_002: My employees did a lot of the work. Maybe I'll take\nthem all to dinner in celebration.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B16_m01: <BLN>This feels amazing!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B17_m01_001: I hope to hear the tale of the legendary bard\nBakhar again.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B17_m01_002: It's a wonderful story, and I think I'd have a new\nappreciation for it now that I'm older.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B17_m01: <BLN>I do hope to hear it again.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B18_m01_001: Books are a fabulous source of knowledge, and that's\nnot all there is to recommend them.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B18_m01_002: They are also an asset in lean times. I keep a room\nfull of them, as they're bound to fetch high prices.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B18_m01: <BLN>Books are a sound investment.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B19_m01_001: To stand upon the stage of the theater in the capital\nand hear the applause ring out is a high honor.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B19_m01_002: But not so high as securing a role in a play by the\nmatchless playwright Dante...
MID_LGA_1_M07_B19_m01: <BLN>The role of a lifetime!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B20_m01_001: Everyone's talking about the priest fighting in the\nHeroic Games while wearing a strange cat mask.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B20_m01_002: Well, her face was revealed after her mask was\nshattered during a match!
MID_LGV_1_M07_B20_m01_003: Even a small glimpse of her beauty was enough to\nleave some people thunderstruck.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B20_m01: <BLN>Her beauty was indescribable...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B21_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B21_m01_001: I heard a story that Dagda the Great had a hundred\nwarships built.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B21_m01_002: Must've been getting ready to fight the Pirate King\nover who got to be boss in the Danann Sea.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B21_m01_003: How come? Well...both those things happened\naround the same time, I think.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B21_m01: <BLN>I'm right about this. I think.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B22_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B22_m01_001: Is it true that the priest with the cat mask is\nastoundingly beautiful?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B22_m01_002: I've heard that young men are flocking to Credna's\ntemple to get a look at her.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B22_m01: <BLN>Absolutely astounding.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B23_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B23_m01_001: In certain parts of Dagda, a being called Pallraven\nis being worshipped in secret.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B23_m01_002: This Pallraven is supposedly older than the Dagdan\npantheon—it was the original faith of this land.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B23_m01_003: It supposedly took the form of a white raven. But\nisn't belief in such things heresy against the temples?
MID_LGA_1_M07_B23_m01: <BLN>Want to hear a secret?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B24_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B24_m01_001: It's when everything is at peace that fears of the\nend of the world flourish.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B24_m01_002: Peace makes us uneasy. We start to wonder just how\nlong it can hold.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B24_m01: <BLN>Perhaps it's a natural reaction.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B25_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B25_m01_001: I don't really know if this story is true or not, so take\nit with a grain of salt.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B25_m01_002: But there's a deadly carriage traveling around Dagda.\nAnyone who gets too close is cut down.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B25_m01_003: The thing is colossal, jet black, and covered in\nsharp spikes.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B25_m01_004: It drives like it owns the roads, knocking aside\nanything that blocks its path.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B25_m01_005: One story even says that it forced another carriage\noff a cliff. What a way to meet one's end!
MID_LGA_1_M07_B25_m01: <BLN>I don't know if it's true, but...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B26_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B26_m01_001: There are two difficult points in the Danann Sea:\nAonghas Strait and Bran Narrows.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B26_m01_002: Between them, they block passage to the seas\nbeyond. No ship has yet broken through.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B26_m01: <BLN>The Danann Sea is inescapable.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B27_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B27_m01_001: The White-Maned Demon fights as if possessed.\nHe grows more untamed with every battle.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B27_m01_002: I worry he might be unwell...
MID_LGA_1_M07_B27_m01: <BLN>The White-Maned Demon...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B28_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B28_m01_001: Have you noticed that the weapons you can use\nchange depending on your class?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B28_m01_002: Each class has some weapons they specialize in,\nand others they're less suited to.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B28_m01_003: Use a favored weapon and you can be sure your skill\nwith it will rapidly increase.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B28_m01_004: Though if you are bent on using a weapon you're less\nproficient with, the results may be disappointing.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B28_m01: <BLN>Are you mindful of your weapons?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B29_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B29_m01_001: There's a theory that Drake's treasures actually call\nout to their own kind.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B29_m01_002: If it's true, we may well be hosting many such\nwielders of the treasures at the Heroic Games.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B29_m01: <BLN>If the theory holds...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B30_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B30_m01_001: There are a few Flame Lords of Dagda who are\nparticularly well-known.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B30_m01_002: There was Unsinkable Gisco, who claimed victory\nat sea against Brigid in the year 875.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B30_m01_003: Caius the Avalanche, who took command at the\nCleansing of Damascar in the year 881.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B30_m01_004: And how can we forget the mighty combatants in the\nDuel for the Gods in the year 1043?
MID_LGV_1_M07_B30_m01_005: The champion Breza and King Hanno, who received\nthe titles Dust-Rage Breza and Red-Ray Hanno.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B30_m01_006: Although in that case, their Flame Lord titles are\nsadly not very widely known today.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B30_m01: <BLN>Among the Flame Lords of Dagda...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B31_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B31_m01_001: Aurora's domain is knowledge of the sea and\nvoyages upon it.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B31_m01_002: That's why sailors and travelers embarking on long\nvoyages often visit her temple before departing.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B31_m01_003: There's talk of the queen of Saramis visiting recently.\nThe story going around is no audience was granted.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B31_m01: <BLN>Aurora's domain is...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B32_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B32_m01_001: The kingdom of Brezarant in the southwest was\nfounded by the champion Breza.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B32_m01_002: Breza was a demigod born of Mars, the Bringer of\nWar, and a human.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B32_m01_003: He fought a storied match in the arena against King\nHanno of Arago, known as the Duel for the Gods.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B32_m01_004: His feats in that battle won him recognition for his\nbudding nation.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B32_m01: <BLN>The kingdom of Brezarant...
MID_LGV_1_M07_B33_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B33_m01_001: Among the Arcs stored in the temples, the Supreme\nArcs are especially noteworthy.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B33_m01_002: These are artifacts of uncanny power, usually bearing\nthe name of one of the divines.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B33_m01_003: On occasion, some people receive special permission\nfrom the gods to wield them.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B33_m01: <BLN>Ah, the Supreme Arcs.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B34_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B34_m01_001: Children born from the union of a god and a human\nhave bloodmarks just like the gods.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B34_m01_002: They're also said to be stronger than ordinary men,\nwith longer lifespans to boot.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B34_m01: <BLN>Gods can procreate with humans.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B35_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B35_m01_001: Honest folk got no business here.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B35_m01_002: So disappear before someone disappears you.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B35_m01: <BLN>Get lost.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B36_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M07_B36_m01_001: There's a commonly held belief about\nDagda's temple.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B36_m01_002: They say vows sworn before that temple have a\npower that endures for eternity.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B36_m01_003: For that reason, young men and women of Dagsion\noften choose that spot to profess their love.
MID_LGV_1_M07_B36_m01_004: Though if the priests catch them at it, they'll be\nchased off.
MID_LGA_1_M07_B36_m01: <BLN>Do you know the legend?